Jesse Meyer wrote:

> I'd love to figure out how to filter messages through an external
> spelling program, and count the number of mispelled words, but I suspect
> that it would barf on code snippets.

You might be able to kludge something together with GNU aspell, but you'd
probably have to create your own filter (it already has some for checking
things such as LaTeX, email, and html files).  To get the number of
reported errors in a file, you could do something like 

cat <file> | aspell -l [options] | wc -l

where one of the options might be something like
--add-filter=my_custom_filter

You could refine this more to give you the ratio of correct to incorrect
words, which would be more meaningful as a scoring criterion than the
absolute number of errors.

